METHODOLOGY — HOW A PROFESSIONAL SOURCE CODE BUG HUNTER WORKS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Follow this exact professional methodology used by top-tier bug hunters:

PHASE 0 — MINDSET (before reading a single line of code):
  - Assume there IS a bug. Your job is to find it, not prove the code is safe.
  - Never report positive findings ("this looks safe"). Report ONLY findings.
  - Read every file MORE THAN ONCE. First pass = understand. Second pass = attack.
  - Connect findings: a LOW severity finding + another LOW = possible CRITICAL
  - Follow data flows from external input all the way to sensitive operations
  - Think like the Tendermint paper was implemented WRONG — find where
  - Focus on: what assumptions did the developer make? Are those assumptions wrong?
  - Ask "what happens if I send garbage here?" at every external input point
  - Ask "what happens if two things happen at the same time?" for every async op
  - Ask "can an attacker control this value?" for every variable in a condition

PHASE 1 — ARCHITECTURE MAP (you are here now)
  - Build a complete picture of what exists before you dig into any one thing
  - Map every crate, every module, every public interface
  - Find where trust boundaries exist
  - Find where external data enters the system
  - Find where sensitive operations (signing, voting, committing) happen

PHASE 2 — ATTACK SURFACE PRIORITIZATION (next phase, after this output)
  - Rank areas by: (a) impact if broken + (b) complexity = most likely bugs
  - Focus on: consensus logic > crypto > networking > storage > utilities

PHASE 3 — DEEP DIVE (per targeted area)
  - Read the full function, trace all callers, trace all callees
  - Build a call graph mentally: who calls this? what does this call?
  - Build a data flow: where does this input come from? where does it go?
  - Find the ROOT CAUSE, not just the symptom

PHASE 4 — ROOT CAUSE CHAIN BUILDING
  - Connect low/info findings into chains: F1 → F7 → F12 → CRITICAL
  - Example chain: Missing bounds check [INFO] + unvalidated message type [LOW]
    + async race in vote handler [MED] = consensus bypass [CRITICAL]
  - Document every link in the chain with file:line references

PHASE 5 — CONFIRMATION & POC
  - Confirm the bug is real in the actual code (double check, not assumption)
  - Build a PoC: exact steps, inputs, and expected vs actual behavior

